  "title": "Erdős Problem #151",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For a graph $G$ let $\\tau(G)$ denote the minimal number of vertices that include at least one from each maximal clique of $G$ on at least two vertices (sometimes called the clique transversal number).\nLet $H(n)$ be maximal such that every triangle-free graph on $n$ vertices contains an independent set on $H(n)$ vertices.\nIf $G$ is a graph on $n$ vertices then is $ \\tau(G)\\leq n-H(n)? $ ",
